cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the article and the archived software."
title: "recovery-evidence: simulation and analysis code for prioritizing recovery-evidence verification under limited audit capacity"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for a paired simulation study of four deterministic
  policies that choose which recovery-evidence record to verify next when
  services share dependencies and the audit budget is fixed. Contains the
  generator (NumPy PCG64, five separated streams), the operator, test-module
  and evaluator separation, the 13 experimental conditions, byte-reproducible
  primary logs, an analysis that does not import the simulator, 27
  implementation checks, figure code and a claim-to-evidence register. All
  results are synthetic model output about the correctness of readiness
  records; they are not measurements of recovery time, loss or compliance.
